Use the installed Windows SDK instead of hardcoded SDK paths.

build/common.gypi wires specific Windows SDK locations into the compiler and
linker settings:

  * Include dirs pin 'Include/10.0.10240.0/{shared,um,winrt}' -- the original
    Windows 10 RTM SDK, which is almost never the one installed.
  * Library dirs pin 'Lib/10.0.10240.0/um/<arch>' for x64, and two of them
    still point at the older 'Lib/win8/um/x86'.
  * '$(VSInstallDir)/VC/atlmfc/include' moved under VC/Tools/MSVC in VS2017.

None of those paths exist on a current VS2022 + SDK 10 machine. They get
prepended to the real ones, so cl and link silently ignore them -- but they are
wrong, they hide which SDK is actually in use, and they are what the VS project
migrator complains about ("could not convert attribute
AdditionalLibraryDirectories ... Windows Kits\8.0\Lib\win8\um\x86").

GYP's msvs generator emits WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, so MSBuild's own
toolset property sheets resolve the SDK and ATL include/library paths. This
drops the hardcoded entries and lets that happen.

The windows_sdk_path variable definition is left in place; nothing references
it now.

Rebased for Chromium 49; the M37 version of this patch targeted the SDK 8.0
paths that release used.

--- a/build/common.gypi
+++ b/build/common.gypi
@@ -3321,18 +3321,14 @@
             # increase this.
             'MinimumRequiredVersion': '5.02',  # Server 2003.
             'TargetMachine': '17', # x86 - 64
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories!':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/10.0.10240.0/um/x86'],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/10.0.10240.0/um/x64'],
+            # PATCHED: SDK library path dropped; MSBuild resolves the SDK
+            # from WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, which GYP emits.
             # Doesn't exist x64 SDK. Should use oleaut32 in any case.
             'IgnoreDefaultLibraryNames': [ 'olepro32.lib' ],
           },
           'VCLibrarianTool': {
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories!':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/10.0.10240.0/um/x86'],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories':
-              ['<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/10.0.10240.0/um/x64'],
+            # PATCHED: SDK library path dropped; MSBuild resolves the SDK
+            # from WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, which GYP emits.
             'TargetMachine': '17', # x64
           },
         },
@@ -5663,10 +5659,11 @@
           }],
         ],
         'msvs_system_include_dirs': [
-          '<(windows_sdk_path)/Include/10.0.10240.0/shared',
-          '<(windows_sdk_path)/Include/10.0.10240.0/um',
-          '<(windows_sdk_path)/Include/10.0.10240.0/winrt',
-          '$(VSInstallDir)/VC/atlmfc/include',
+          # PATCHED: these pinned Windows SDK 10.0.10240.0 -- the original
+          # Windows 10 RTM SDK, which is not what is installed. ATL also moved
+          # under VC/Tools/MSVC in VS2017, so $(VSInstallDir)/VC/atlmfc is
+          # wrong too. GYP emits WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, so MSBuild's
+          # toolset property sheets supply the right SDK and ATL paths.
         ],
         'msvs_cygwin_shell': 0,
         'msvs_disabled_warnings': [
@@ -5761,9 +5758,8 @@
           },
           'VCLibrarianTool': {
             'AdditionalOptions': ['/ignore:4221'],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories': [
-              '<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x86',
-            ],
+            # PATCHED: SDK library path dropped; MSBuild resolves the SDK
+            # from WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, which GYP emits.
           },
           'VCLinkerTool': {
             'AdditionalDependencies': [
@@ -5778,9 +5774,8 @@
               'winmm.lib',
               'shlwapi.lib',
             ],
-            'AdditionalLibraryDirectories': [
-              '<(windows_sdk_path)/Lib/win8/um/x86',
-            ],
+            # PATCHED: SDK library path dropped; MSBuild resolves the SDK
+            # from WindowsTargetPlatformVersion, which GYP emits.
             'GenerateDebugInformation': 'true',
             'MapFileName': '$(OutDir)\\$(TargetName).map',
             'FixedBaseAddress': '1',
